---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
        title="Capabilities — Means+Measures"
        description="Means+Measures capabilities for civic infrastructure, public information systems, records, AI governance, and document-forward analysis."
>
    <section class="section">
        <p class="eyebrow">Capabilities</p>

        <div class="measure">
            <h1>What Means+Measures can build.</h1>
            <p>
                Means+Measures works where public information, institutional process, and human consequence meet.
                The useful work is usually not a louder dashboard. It is a better record, a clearer route,
                a more honest interface, or an infrastructure layer that lets responsibility travel upward.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-list">
            <section>
                <h2>Civic information infrastructure</h2>
                <p>
                    Resource directories, public data surfaces, correction workflows, practical access guidance,
                    multilingual navigation, and machine-readable exports for communities and public partners.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Records and review systems</h2>
                <p>
                    Record-sufficiency reviews, public-comment support, procurement packets, public-record
                    organization, artifact publication, and systems that keep decisions inspectable.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>AI governance and memory</h2>
                <p>
                    Governed agent-memory patterns, provenance review, stop lifecycle design, attributable
                    state transitions, and practical controls for AI-mediated workflows.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Observational data systems</h2>
                <p>
                    Source-faithful ingestion, temporal integrity, geo-resolved observations, public-interest
                    telemetry, and data models built for downstream analysis without erasing provenance.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Plain-language institutional interfaces</h2>
                <p>
                    Intake forms, guidance pages, process maps, public notices, and accessibility-forward
                    content that gives people enough information to make real decisions.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="measure">
            <p class="document-action">
                For institutional coordination, use <a href="/procurement">procurement</a>. For exploratory work,
                use <a href="/contact">contact</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
